incident-bot: INCIDENT: spike in 5xx and tail latency on /v1/generate (us-west-2) detected at 09:12 UTC. Auto-escalating to oncall.
alex: I'm on metrics + traces. seeing queue depth increase on runtime pool 3.
maria: streaming connections are up 3x since 09:10, embeddings write throughput also spiking from a handful of customers.
kevin: repro locally with simulated fanout: a client opening 30 short requests concurrently causes KV cache pressure -> CPU steal.
alex: immediate mitigation plan: 1) apply per-client token-bucket rate limit (burst 100, rate 10rps) 2) reduce per-customer concurrency to 50 3) disable streaming chunks for affected model in us-west-2. I'll apply 1+2 now.
deploy-bot: flag update: streaming_chunks_enabled=false (prod-us-west-2) by alex @ 09:22 UTC — rollout 2/2 hosts updated. :white_check_mark:
emma: we should push a short SDK advisory now: reduce default retries, add exponential backoff + jitter, require idempotency header for operations that can be retried. Customers should also surface Retry-After from 429s.
kevin: agree. SDK changes (short): - default maxRetries -> 2 - baseBackoff -> 200ms - maxBackoff -> 10s - jitter -> full jitter - include Idempotency-Key header optional for POSTs
kevin: example JS snippet to include in advisory:
```js
// recommended client-side retry (JS)
async function retryWithBackoff(fn, maxRetries = 2) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (true) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      attempt++;
      if (attempt > maxRetries) throw err;
      const base = 200 * Math.pow(2, attempt - 1);
      const wait = Math.min(10000, base);
      const jitter = Math.random() * wait;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, jitter));
    }
  }
}
```
maria: also add guidance: avoid per-user fanout spikes — encourage request batching and shared connection pools. For streaming-heavy customers, recommend switching to polling with larger chunks for now.
alex: customer-impact: enterprise customers X & Y seeing degraded tail latency and occasional 503s on streaming; smaller users mostly unaffected. CS please notify.
customer-success: CC'ing account teams for X and Y now, sending a consolidated note with workaround (disable streaming, reduce client concurrency).
oncall: handoff note for night shift: mitigations applied are token-bucket + concurrency cap + streaming disabled. SDK advisory drafted, will post to #devex and update SDK release notes with immediate hotfix. Please watch error-rate dashboards and autoscaling queue depth.
sre-ops: added a temporary routing rule to divert traffic to us-east fallback if us-west spikes > 20% error rate. Keep an eye on cross-region capacity.
alex: longer-term backlog items: - automated per-customer backpressure signals to the SDK (soft-429) - server-side connection-level flow-control - improved telemetry for client fanout patterns
emma: publishing advisory to SDK channels and creating a short snippet for quick copy-paste into customer repos. Will include explicit handling for 429 Retry-After and not retrying on random 5xx except 502/503 with backoff.
kevin: follow-up: add a client header X-Idempotency-Key suggestion + sample server response for duplicate detection.
alex: closing note: mitigations look stable at 09:40 UTC, latency trending down. We'll start a 2-hour post-incident watch and update the thread if anything regresses. :thumbsup:
customer-success: customers X and Y acknowledged workaround, will monitor.
oncall: handing off to night oncall @ 18:00 UTC — full mitigation notes are in ops runbook (internal link). If errors spike again, escalate to eng-runtime immediately.
